<title>UK: Caird helped to H1 pretax profit by exceps.</title>
<headline>Caird helped to H1 pretax profit by exceps.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) (diluted)  28.78 earnings     vs 13.59 loss</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.0		    vs n/a</p>
<p> Pretax		     7.98 profit	  vs 0.55 loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   9.93		   vs 7.67</p>
<p> Operating result	 1.63		   vs 0.34</p>
<p> Exceptional		6.68		   vs nil</p>
<p> Interest		   0.33		   vs 0.89</p>
<p> Tax			  0.15		   vs nil</p>
<p> Net taxed		  7.83 profit	  vs 0.55 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 24</p>
<p>Div registration date  September 24  Ex-div date		September 16</p>
<p>Note - Landfill and waste management group Caird Group Plc said it expected the overall result for the year to be good and &quot;confidently expects to declare a final dividend.&quot; The exceptional item comprised a bank waiver as part of a reconstruction agreement less associated costs. Earnings per share exclude exceptional items.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
